  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TFM - Skills for Elderly &amp; Youth Farmers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Full Project title: Boost, Amplify, Nurture, &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Deepen (BAND) Elderly and Youth farmers skills for a stronger and rights-holder driven organization and empowered leaders

The main changes that we want to highlight and expand on are: (1)increase in the numberof farmer RH who have accessed resources from the state or government, such as increased in the number Senior Citizens who have received social pension provided by the LGU. For instance, in the precious project was successful in its engagement with the LGU of Silay. Mayor Gallego of Silay committed to provide Php 600 per month social pension for 3,900 farmer petitioners. In addition, one of the resources that we want the rights holders to claim are various agricultural support services that government agencies can provideas well as prepare qualified RH to become suppliers to a Muscovado facility, in order for the Senior Citizens and youth to improve their livelihood; (2) We also target further strengthening of the 2 registered RH organization and so that it will be able to gain provincial recognition and influence. (3) We aim for this project to be able to integrate the RH (Sc and Youth) in a social media platform that the RH would be able to directly create their stories, promote their advocacies,and get direct feedback from their audience. This project also wants to accomplish both change from the individual rights-holder and organizational transformation. This empowerment accelerator project hopes to deepen or sharpen the capacities of rights-holder and further strengthen their organizations. The EM accelerator program will build on the accomplishment of the previous Voice project, which already reached more than 30 community organizations or peoples&#x2019; organization in Negros Occidental and with 2DOLE-registered organization composed of Senior Citizens and Youth members. In terms of individual rights holders, at the end of the project, we hope to have (1) well-informed rights-holders,senior citizens and youth, of their rights based on governmentpolicies and agency programs, (2) skilled RH in terms of articulatingtheir advocacies in various platforms, (3) key RH officers possessing leadership and management skills; (4) individual RH actively facilitating collaborations and negotiations with government agencies and stakeholders; (5) as well as individual RH actively participating as suppliers to a Muscovado facility in La Castellana, or similar facility in Negros Occidental. In terms of organizational change, we hope the project would results to: (1) strong RH organization that is managed by its own set of officers and thus able todevelop its own programs for its RH members, (2) an organization that established partnership and collaboration with municipal and provincial Offices of the Senior Citizens, (3) an organization that is also recognized at the provincial level to represent themselves at dialogues and consultations with government bodies.</narrative>
  </description>
